{
  "outcome": "needs_user_info",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Sofia, sorry your computer is acting up again. I'd like to get this fixed, but I need a bit more detail first. Could you tell me: 1) What exactly happens? For example, is it slow, freezing, crashing or showing a blue screen, not connecting to Wi-Fi or VPN, or not printing? 2) Do you see an error message? If so, what does it say? A screenshot or photo is great. 3) When did it start this time, and does anything seem to set it off, like a certain app, waking it from sleep, or plugging in a dock? 4) When did you last fully restart it (Start > Power > Restart, not just closing the lid)? Also, our system shows your laptop hasn't connected to the company network in about 12 days. If you can, please connect it to the office network or VPN and restart it so it can pick up updates. Once I hear back, I'll take it from there.",
  "internal_note": "Ticket is vague: 'doing the thing again', no symptoms given, and I can't see any earlier tickets to tell what 'the thing' is. User: Sofia Rossi (id 7), Marketing, account active, 0 failed logins, not blocked, mailbox 27.9% used. Device BL-LT-0107 (Win 11 Pro): offline, last check-in 2026-09-29, warning 'No check-in for 12 days'. Disk is fine (54.7% free), so low disk space (KB-017) is ruled out. The 12-day gap without a check-in could be part of the problem, or the laptop may just have been off or away from the network. Asked the user for symptoms, error text, when it started, and last restart. Next step: match her answer to the right article (KB-019 if it's slow or freezing). Escalate if she reports blue screens or repeated crashes, or if the check-in gap points to an agent or network problem. If you know of an earlier ticket from this user, it may explain what 'the thing' is.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-019",
    "KB-017"
  ],
  "confidence": "medium"
}
